Package: missBART
Type: Package
Title: Joint Models for Non-Ignorable Missing Responses using Bayesian Additive Regression Trees
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(person("Yong Chen", "Goh", email="yong.goh.2022@mumail.ie", role=c("aut", "cre")),
  person("Keefe", "Murphy", email="keefe.murphy@mu.ie", role=c("aut"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7709-3159")),
  person("Andrew", "Parnell", email="andrew.parnell@mu.ie", role=c("aut"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7956-7939")))
Description: Selection models for multivariate responses with missing values
    that may be missing not at random (MNAR). The responses follow a
    multivariate Bayesian additive regression trees (BART) model, and the
    missingness indicators follow either a multivariate probit regression
    ('missBART1') or a multivariate probit BART model ('missBART2') in which
    the responses themselves are predictors, so that missing completely at
    random, missing at random and MNAR mechanisms can all be recovered. Missing
    responses are imputed as part of the Markov chain Monte Carlo scheme. The
    samplers are written in 'C++'. The methods are described in Goh, Soh,
    Parnell and Murphy (2024) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2412.14946>.
